#: ../../../hacking.rst:6
msgid "Where the build backend lives"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../hacking.rst:10
msgid ""
"The classic build backend was removed; a few internal modules survive as "
"deprecated shims."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../hacking.rst:13
msgid ""
"The build backend is provided by the setuptools plugin of `scikit-build-core "
"<https://scikit-build-core.readthedocs.io>`_; ``skbuild`` is a thin wrapper "
"around it that re-exports ``setup()`` and ships the scikit-build CMake "
"modules. If you want to hack on how projects are configured and built, look "
"at the `scikit-build-core repository <https://github.com/scikit-build/scikit-"
"build-core>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../hacking.rst:20
msgid ""
"The public Python API is ``skbuild.setup`` and ``skbuild.exceptions."
"SKBuildError``. Anything else is deprecated: ``skbuild.cmaker``, ``skbuild."
"constants``, ``skbuild.utils`` and ``skbuild.setuptools_wrap`` are "
"compatibility shims that warn on import and keep only the handful of helpers "
"downstream ``setup.py`` files use (see below)."
msgstr ""

